WEBVTT

00:00:45.546 --> 00:00:48.799
<i>An unknown frontier</i>

00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:52.386
<i>On the map painted by my heart</i>

00:00:52.386 --> 00:00:59.142
<i>When I open the door, the path goes on</i>

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:05.107
<i>I'm kicking up dust as I</i>
<i>start running to your town</i>

00:01:05.107 --> 00:01:11.822
<i>Along a route where earth and sky meet</i>

00:01:11.822 --> 00:01:15.576
<i>Riding the rushing southern wind</i>

00:01:15.576 --> 00:01:18.495
<i>Slicing through the wind</i>
<i>dyed blue by the sky</i>

00:01:18.495 --> 00:01:25.627
<i>I'm rushing out with my whole heart</i>

00:01:25.627 --> 00:01:29.131
<i>Shooting past the midday moon</i>

00:01:29.131 --> 00:01:32.259
<i>Towards a world different</i>
<i>from what we've known before</i>

00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:36.096
<i>I will keep on running through to the end</i>

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.681
<i>However far</i>

00:01:37.681 --> 00:01:41.602
<i>Just like that wind</i>

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:46.899
<i>Just like that wind</i>

00:02:11.298 --> 00:02:13.842
You fell for it, Kumodoshin
or whatever you call yourself.

00:02:13.842 --> 00:02:15.844
Now I've got you trapped like a rat!

00:02:15.844 --> 00:02:19.431
What do you think you can
do against this many people?

00:02:19.431 --> 00:02:21.642
Run, Lord Kumodoshin!

00:02:21.642 --> 00:02:25.646
Silence, impudent wench!

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:32.402
You bastard...

00:02:32.402 --> 00:02:34.696
Kill him, men!

00:02:34.696 --> 00:02:36.156
Kill him!

00:02:41.537 --> 00:02:44.289
We interrupt your regularly
scheduled program...

00:02:44.289 --> 00:02:46.500
--Come on, that was the best part!
--...to bring you a special news bulletin...

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.794
--The news can wait a measly three minutes!
--At 1:00 PM Japan time,

00:02:48.794 --> 00:02:49.044
--That was Detarame Dacchanbaru's
--At 1:00 PM Japan time,

00:02:49.044 --> 00:02:50.254
--That was Detarame Dacchanbaru's
--there was a large explosion

00:02:50.254 --> 00:02:50.754
--ultimate scene!
--there was a large explosion

00:02:50.754 --> 00:02:52.005
--ultimate scene!
--at the assembly hall in Nanking where the

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.048
--But this appears to be very important news.
--at the assembly hall in Nanking where the

00:02:53.048 --> 00:02:54.967
--But this appears to be very important news.
--North-South peace conference was being held.

00:02:54.967 --> 00:02:57.344
--How can you say that?
--The number of casualties is unknown.

00:02:57.344 --> 00:02:57.594
--How can you say that?
--Currently, a group calling themselves

00:02:57.594 --> 00:02:59.012
--This is "The Amazing Kumodoshin"!
--Currently, a group calling themselves

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.013
--This is "The Amazing Kumodoshin"!
--"The Lost 500,000 Men"...

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:02.724
--This is Uruz 7.
--It's a super-rare period drama that was only

00:03:02.724 --> 00:03:03.016
--This is Uruz 7.
--broadcast for three months back in Showa 56!

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:04.351
--I just found out.
--broadcast for three months back in Showa 56!

00:03:04.351 --> 00:03:04.726
--It's already being reported on.
--broadcast for three months back in Showa 56!

00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:06.311
--It's already being reported on.
--It's almost a miracle

00:03:06.311 --> 00:03:06.562
--It's already being reported on.
--that it's even being re-run!

00:03:06.562 --> 00:03:08.105
--Roger. Code 3.
--that it's even being re-run!

00:03:08.105 --> 00:03:08.355
--Roger. Code 3.
--Some fans who want this on DVD...

00:03:08.355 --> 00:03:10.440
--I'll head there immediately via Route B2.
--Some fans who want this on DVD...

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:13.026
Hey, Sousuke, are you listening?

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:14.570
Some urgent business has just come up.

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:15.737
What urgent business?

00:03:15.737 --> 00:03:16.947
I'll return the day after tomorrow.

00:03:16.947 --> 00:03:18.699
What? Where are you going?

00:03:18.699 --> 00:03:21.869
We have a math quiz tomorrow, you know!

00:03:21.869 --> 00:03:24.746
Be sure to go straight home if you can.

00:03:24.746 --> 00:03:25.789
Huh?

00:03:25.789 --> 00:03:27.916
Wait... Sousuke!

00:03:27.916 --> 00:03:29.459
--According to the announcement
by the local police,

00:03:29.459 --> 00:03:30.043
--He left. Jeez...
--According to the announcement by the local police,

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:32.045
--He left. Jeez...
--the armed group which abducted the North China Diplomatic Corps

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:33.130
--the armed group which abducted
the North China Diplomatic Corps

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:35.465
is equipped with at least five AS units,

00:03:35.465 --> 00:03:39.052
and is currently engaged in a
battle inside the city of Nanking.

00:03:40.512 --> 00:03:43.807
"The Labyrinth and the Dragon"

00:03:59.406 --> 00:04:03.327
That's it. Keep firing away...

00:04:03.327 --> 00:04:06.288
Fireworks should be big,
and asses should be small.

00:04:06.288 --> 00:04:08.081
"Asses," sir?

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:09.917
It doesn't really mean anything.

00:04:11.835 --> 00:04:13.504
"Halt! Otherwise..."

00:04:13.504 --> 00:04:15.672
"Otherwise,"

00:04:15.672 --> 00:04:16.882
"this will happen!"

00:04:30.437 --> 00:04:31.980
Gates has broken through!

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:34.775
He's no mere racer; his moves are pure<i> art</i>!

00:04:36.401 --> 00:04:38.862
The machines are rounding the final corner!

00:04:38.862 --> 00:04:40.614
The audience is going wild!

00:04:40.614 --> 00:04:43.617
Will he make it? Can he make it?

00:04:43.617 --> 00:04:46.119
The Nanking Grand Prix
is now in its final stretch!

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:47.746
Ow.

00:04:47.746 --> 00:04:50.165
It's dangerous, sir, so please wear a helmet.

00:04:50.165 --> 00:04:52.584
I hate 'em.

00:04:52.584 --> 00:04:54.461
They make me go bald.

00:05:01.468 --> 00:05:04.680
The ceasefire summit between
North and South China

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:07.391
was attacked by an
armed terrorist group.

00:05:07.391 --> 00:05:08.600
Seven hours ago

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:12.145
in Nanking, a city in the Yangtze River basin...

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:13.897
I apologize for being late.

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:22.906
Three AS units attacked the assembly hall,

00:05:22.906 --> 00:05:24.157
and they abducted five individuals

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:27.828
who were part of or associated with the
North China Diplomatic Corps.

00:05:27.828 --> 00:05:29.663
The members of this armed
group put up fierce resistance

00:05:29.663 --> 00:05:30.998
as they escaped via an overland route,

00:05:30.998 --> 00:05:32.833
and they are currently
holding their position

00:05:32.833 --> 00:05:34.626
in the depths of the
Cross-Yangtze River Tunnel.

00:05:34.626 --> 00:05:38.172
They are calling themselves
"The Lost 500,000 Men,"

00:05:38.172 --> 00:05:41.175
but the existence of such a terrorist
organization has not yet been confirmed.

00:05:41.175 --> 00:05:44.720
We already have them surrounded, and...

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:45.971
Captain.

00:05:45.971 --> 00:05:47.222
Yes?

00:05:47.222 --> 00:05:49.433
Are you in accord with
everything I've said so far?

00:05:49.433 --> 00:05:51.935
Yes. Please continue.

00:05:51.935 --> 00:05:53.020
Yes, ma'am.

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:56.523
This is the location the
terrorist group is holding.

00:05:56.523 --> 00:05:58.859
The Cross-Yangtze River Tunnel in Nanking.

00:05:58.859 --> 00:06:00.903
It spans four kilometers.

00:06:00.903 --> 00:06:04.823
It can safely be considered the
largest man-made structure in the region.

00:06:04.823 --> 00:06:07.826
This is where we will
conduct our rescue operation.

00:06:09.161 --> 00:06:10.829
Sure is big.

00:06:10.829 --> 00:06:13.665
And complex.

00:06:13.665 --> 00:06:17.586
This tunnel was constructed using the
previous generation of technology,

00:06:17.586 --> 00:06:20.631
and its specifications were modified
several times due to the civil war.

00:06:20.631 --> 00:06:22.841
Because of this, there are numerous
shafts and inclined passages,

00:06:22.841 --> 00:06:25.511
giving it an extremely complicated structure.

00:06:25.511 --> 00:06:28.889
It's a tunnel in name only.
It seems more like a dungeon to me.

00:06:28.889 --> 00:06:31.934
Exactly. You could say it's a kind of labyrinth.

00:06:31.934 --> 00:06:34.061
With the exception of some of the work shafts,

00:06:34.061 --> 00:06:37.606
everything is wide enough for an
AS to execute tactical operations.

00:06:37.606 --> 00:06:41.527
Six enemy AS Savages are probably
waiting in ambush in several locations.

00:06:41.527 --> 00:06:42.986
There are most likely traps as well.

00:06:42.986 --> 00:06:45.239
Local forces do not have
sufficient equipment to handle this.

00:06:45.239 --> 00:06:49.243
Piece of cake. We've got M9s.

00:06:49.243 --> 00:06:51.662
I hope it'll be that easy.

00:06:51.662 --> 00:06:55.791
First, we will have three infantry squads
infiltrate the location from these points.

00:06:55.791 --> 00:06:58.794
Once the route has been secured,
three AS units will move in.

00:06:58.794 --> 00:07:02.047
The AS team will consist of
Mao, Weber, and Sagara.

00:07:02.047 --> 00:07:04.550
The rest will be under the
command of their respective squads.

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:05.592
Given the nature of the location,

00:07:05.592 --> 00:07:08.262
the use of high-caliber artillery and
ammunition, guided missiles, and sniping

00:07:08.262 --> 00:07:10.264
are all completely infeasible.

00:07:10.264 --> 00:07:12.182
We must be careful about
our communications, too.

00:07:12.182 --> 00:07:16.937
You have been given a list of all confirmed
information regarding enemy equipment, etc.

00:07:16.937 --> 00:07:18.146
It's all tentative.

00:07:18.146 --> 00:07:21.316
Why don't you stop giving us these
handouts and just send us the data?

00:07:21.316 --> 00:07:25.028
Once we confirm the specific location
where the hostages are being held,

00:07:25.028 --> 00:07:28.282
we will provide you with
timetables and details on the routes.

00:07:28.282 --> 00:07:30.951
Memorize the arrangement
and lengths of the shafts.

00:07:30.951 --> 00:07:32.619
And I mean thoroughly.

00:07:32.619 --> 00:07:36.874
But these figures don't
even agree with each other!

00:07:36.874 --> 00:07:39.960
It even says here that this
description isn't accurate.

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:42.713
Does that mean this one's a lie too?

00:07:42.713 --> 00:07:44.923
This is just like the Cretans' paradox.

00:07:44.923 --> 00:07:46.049
What's that?

00:07:46.049 --> 00:07:49.303
It's the paradox that's created when a
Cretan says, "All Cretans are liars."

00:07:49.303 --> 00:07:53.807
It's impossible to prove it true or false.

00:07:53.807 --> 00:07:57.311
Save the lecture on Epimenides for later.

00:07:57.311 --> 00:08:00.606
Moving on, Intelligence has
dispatched an engineer

00:08:00.606 --> 00:08:04.568
to meet you on site in order to secure
communication in the tunnels.

00:08:04.568 --> 00:08:06.778
His name is Captain Vincent Bruno.

00:08:06.778 --> 00:08:08.655
He will probably give
you an explanation

00:08:08.655 --> 00:08:11.325
regarding the use of the
transmitters prior to the operation.

00:08:11.325 --> 00:08:12.326
Roger.

00:08:12.326 --> 00:08:13.160
Yes sir.

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:14.703
--Yes, sir.
--Yes, sir.

00:08:14.703 --> 00:08:16.663
That concludes my briefing.

00:08:16.663 --> 00:08:18.665
Captain, if you please.

00:08:18.665 --> 00:08:19.750
Yes.

00:08:26.256 --> 00:08:28.550
Considering the international
attention on this incident,

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:30.677
This operation is considerably
more delicate than

00:08:30.677 --> 00:08:33.347
the one in the
Khanka Autonomous Region.

00:08:33.347 --> 00:08:35.682
Because the area of
operation is located inland,

00:08:35.682 --> 00:08:38.894
we will be unable to provide
you with rapid support.

00:08:38.894 --> 00:08:42.356
There is a similar situation described
in my report "Theoretical Exercises,"

00:08:42.356 --> 00:08:44.900
which was distributed on the
28th of last month,

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:47.194
so please read it again carefully.

00:08:47.194 --> 00:08:50.989
However, you are all both
highly-skilled and well-equipped.

00:08:50.989 --> 00:08:52.991
Complete this assignment
in your usual manner,

00:08:52.991 --> 00:08:56.370
and I am sure you will be back
in time for lunch tomorrow.

00:08:56.370 --> 00:09:00.040
That is all. Any questions?

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:01.041
Very well.

00:09:01.041 --> 00:09:04.878
Then please make preparations
in accordance with the prescribed procedure.

00:09:04.878 --> 00:09:06.088
I wish you luck.

00:09:06.088 --> 00:09:07.381
Dismissed.

00:09:34.283 --> 00:09:35.784
Captain Bruno.

00:09:35.784 --> 00:09:37.411
We will be above Nanking shortly.

00:09:37.411 --> 00:09:39.079
Please fasten your seatbelt.

00:09:39.079 --> 00:09:40.664
Yeah.

00:09:59.683 --> 00:10:02.102
All preparations complete.

00:10:14.615 --> 00:10:19.369
Also, the specs for the VRL-108 have
not been proven in this environment.

00:10:19.369 --> 00:10:21.288
--Lieutenant Commander.
--Just a moment.

00:10:21.288 --> 00:10:24.374
Do not change these settings.
Ask Sachs about anything else.

00:10:24.374 --> 00:10:25.959
Understood!

00:10:25.959 --> 00:10:26.960
Lieutenant Commander,

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:29.004
I would like permission to
use an M9 for this mission.

00:10:29.004 --> 00:10:30.047
Denied.

00:10:30.047 --> 00:10:34.092
Please tell me why I absolutely must
use the Arbalest for this mission.

00:10:34.092 --> 00:10:39.473
First, give me a reason why you shouldn't.

00:10:39.473 --> 00:10:40.766
Well...

00:10:40.766 --> 00:10:42.809
Its performance meets our standards.

00:10:42.809 --> 00:10:45.479
If you look at it objectively,
you shouldn't have any complaints.

00:10:45.479 --> 00:10:46.480
Understood.

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:50.150
Also, about the report I submitted to you...

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:51.485
About Wraith?

00:10:51.485 --> 00:10:52.945
Please consider it.

00:10:52.945 --> 00:10:55.822
I cannot believe that a bodyguard
from the Intelligence Division

00:10:55.822 --> 00:10:58.742
is adequately protecting
Chidori in my absence.

00:10:58.742 --> 00:10:59.910
It's as if Wraith's...

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:01.995
...just an observer?

00:11:01.995 --> 00:11:03.038
Yes.

00:11:03.038 --> 00:11:04.831
We are the Tactical Division.

00:11:04.831 --> 00:11:06.959
Our jurisdiction is entirely
different from Intelligence.

00:11:06.959 --> 00:11:08.043
But, sir...

00:11:08.043 --> 00:11:12.214
We have our own battle to fight.
Focus on the operation ahead of you.

00:11:12.214 --> 00:11:13.924
Yes, sir.

00:11:13.924 --> 00:11:15.759
This is the captain speaking.

00:11:15.759 --> 00:11:19.847
This ship will be surfacing
momentarily off the shore of Tontai.

00:11:19.847 --> 00:11:23.183
Please begin your final preparations to deploy.

00:11:23.183 --> 00:11:26.353
We're almost to the
rendezvous point with the engineer.

00:11:26.353 --> 00:11:29.022
A divided China, huh?

00:11:29.022 --> 00:11:31.817
Remind me, how many years
has it been since the civil war,

00:11:31.817 --> 00:11:33.193
when it got divided into North and South?

00:11:33.193 --> 00:11:34.444
Eight years.

00:11:34.444 --> 00:11:38.031
And it's been almost five years
since the armistice agreement.

00:11:38.031 --> 00:11:40.868
The negotiations that
began in Nanking yesterday

00:11:40.868 --> 00:11:43.078
were meant to extend that agreement.

00:11:43.078 --> 00:11:44.538
Jeez, at least watch the news.

00:11:44.538 --> 00:11:46.540
So that's why they were attacked...

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:49.543
Talk about lousy security.

00:11:49.543 --> 00:11:53.589
It wasn't the security that was abnormal,
it was the attackers.

00:11:53.589 --> 00:11:55.382
You've got that right.

00:11:55.382 --> 00:11:57.509
Not only that, but the
Cross-Yangtze River Tunnel

00:11:57.509 --> 00:12:00.512
is a neutral zone between
North and South China.

00:12:00.512 --> 00:12:03.056
It's a politically sensitive area.

00:12:03.056 --> 00:12:05.017
One of the topics to be
discussed at that meeting

00:12:05.017 --> 00:12:08.353
was the conflict over the
management of the tunnel.

00:12:08.353 --> 00:12:10.480
Which makes for a very
complicated situation, I see.

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:14.568
Right. That's probably why we were called.

00:12:14.568 --> 00:12:17.029
Moderates from both governments,

00:12:17.029 --> 00:12:20.407
as well as the doves in America
and Russia who are backing them,

00:12:20.407 --> 00:12:24.036
must have unofficially
asked Mithril to stand by.

00:12:24.036 --> 00:12:27.039
After all, if anything
should happen to those hostages,

00:12:27.039 --> 00:12:30.209
it would completely disrupt the negotiations
to extend the armistice agreement.

00:12:30.209 --> 00:12:32.419
With it being five years
since the civil war ended,

00:12:32.419 --> 00:12:34.588
and with both sides finally stabilizing,

00:12:34.588 --> 00:12:36.673
something like that happening
now would cause a lot of problems.

00:12:36.673 --> 00:12:37.549
Simple, isn't it?

00:12:37.549 --> 00:12:39.551
Not at all!

00:12:39.551 --> 00:12:40.969
No, it's quite simple.

00:12:40.969 --> 00:12:42.971
If we fail in our operation,

00:12:42.971 --> 00:12:45.307
there is a danger that
civil war will break out again.

00:12:45.307 --> 00:12:46.475
That's all there is to it.

00:12:46.475 --> 00:12:48.268
Exactly right.

00:12:48.268 --> 00:12:51.063
Then why didn't you just
tell me that in the beginning?

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:54.608
I was getting tired of waiting for you.

00:12:54.608 --> 00:12:57.361
I'm Captain Vincent Bruno,
from Intelligence.

00:12:57.361 --> 00:12:59.321
I'm Sergeant Major Melissa Mao.

00:12:59.321 --> 00:13:00.280
Where's the equipment?

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:02.908
Right here. I'll turn it over to you now.

00:13:04.493 --> 00:13:05.577
As I'm sure you know,

00:13:05.577 --> 00:13:09.498
normal methods of communication
are almost useless within a tunnel.

00:13:09.498 --> 00:13:13.377
You will need to set relay devices
in appropriate locations.

00:13:13.377 --> 00:13:14.628
What's the range?

00:13:14.628 --> 00:13:17.172
Without obstructions, 500 meters.

00:13:17.172 --> 00:13:21.260
But in that maze, 200 meters
is going to be about the limit.

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:23.720
I assume you've supplied
enough relay devices.

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:26.682
Will we be able to
relay back to the Danaan?

00:13:26.682 --> 00:13:30.310
Yeah. I'll assume
responsibility for that relay.

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:32.229
Please leave it to me.

00:13:32.229 --> 00:13:34.481
Understood. We're counting on you.

00:13:43.824 --> 00:13:45.993
"This is Star 1. The path is clear."

00:13:47.327 --> 00:13:49.079
"Now proceeding to Point 4..."

00:13:53.208 --> 00:13:54.001
"Abort! Abort!"

00:13:54.001 --> 00:13:56.420
"It's an enemy trap!
Call the engineering unit immedi..."

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:57.462
"Dammit! They're shooting at me!"

00:13:57.462 --> 00:13:59.590
"It's hopeless! We can't handle them!
At this rate..."

00:14:04.011 --> 00:14:06.930
"All units: Abort mission!
Abort mission!"

00:14:06.930 --> 00:14:08.891
"Abort? But..."

00:14:08.891 --> 00:14:09.766
"Have all units fall back!"

00:14:09.766 --> 00:14:11.393
"The 'specialists' are
going to be handling this one."

00:14:11.393 --> 00:14:13.353
"Understood? Fall back!
Leave this up to 'them.'"

00:14:14.271 --> 00:14:16.523
Uruz 2 to all units.

00:14:16.523 --> 00:14:19.026
Some idiots started the party without us.

00:14:19.026 --> 00:14:22.237
Let's show them who's
playing the lead here! Got it?

00:14:22.237 --> 00:14:23.280
Roger.

00:14:24.698 --> 00:14:29.036
This is Uruz 7. Descent successful.
I'm in the labyrinth.

00:14:29.036 --> 00:14:31.997
Currently heading fast toward Point 02-02.

00:14:31.997 --> 00:14:35.042
Incoming AS. 11 o'clock.
Distance, 3.

00:14:35.042 --> 00:14:36.543
Let's get this done.

00:14:36.543 --> 00:14:37.377
Roger.

00:14:41.256 --> 00:14:42.549
It has begun.

00:14:42.549 --> 00:14:44.009
Yes.

00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:19.336
This is Uruz 2.
Descent successful.

00:15:19.336 --> 00:15:20.754
I've destroyed one Savage.

00:15:20.754 --> 00:15:23.257
Now proceeding to Point 01-14.

00:15:26.093 --> 00:15:29.096
This is Uruz 6.
Descent successful.

00:15:29.096 --> 00:15:30.472
I have...

00:15:31.765 --> 00:15:33.350
...disabled an approaching Savage.

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:34.476
I'm going to finish it off.

00:15:36.353 --> 00:15:40.107
This is Team Ruby.
We've passed Point 03-07.

00:15:40.107 --> 00:15:42.317
No enemies spotted.
No casualties.

00:15:42.317 --> 00:15:46.613
Now proceeding to Point 03-08, as planned.

00:15:46.613 --> 00:15:48.782
Damn, this static is horrible.

00:15:51.326 --> 00:15:53.120
Hey!

00:15:58.292 --> 00:15:59.626
Scary...

00:16:08.343 --> 00:16:11.638
This is Uruz 7.
I've neutralized a second enemy AS.

00:16:11.638 --> 00:16:14.808
Now heading to Point 02-08.

00:16:14.808 --> 00:16:18.812
Due to the large number of obstacles,
the communication line is malfunctioning.

00:16:18.812 --> 00:16:20.314
I know.

00:16:20.314 --> 00:16:22.649
Uruz 7 to Ogma 1.

00:16:22.649 --> 00:16:25.903
Communication is bad.
Is it possible to improve it?

00:16:25.903 --> 00:16:29.156
This is Ogma 1.
This should be enough.

00:16:29.156 --> 00:16:31.533
There is no need for improvement.

00:16:31.533 --> 00:16:33.410
But if something unexpected should happen...

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:35.787
Then I will adjust things appropriately.

00:16:35.787 --> 00:16:37.623
Over and out.

00:16:40.209 --> 00:16:43.712
Two 20mm class sentry guns detected.

00:16:43.712 --> 00:16:45.839
Activate ECS, Stealth Mode.

00:16:45.839 --> 00:16:46.840
Roger.

00:16:53.013 --> 00:16:56.975
This is Uruz 2. I just passed Point 02-15.

00:16:56.975 --> 00:16:59.937
I will now head over to cover Ruby and Topaz.

00:16:59.937 --> 00:17:03.690
This is Uruz 6. Traps found at Point 03-18.

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:06.318
Unable to circumvent.
Heading to 02-18 instead.

00:17:06.318 --> 00:17:11.657
This is Uruz 7. Passed Point 02-09,
proceeding to Point 02-10.

00:17:11.657 --> 00:17:14.201
The neutralization of enemy AS
units is progressing nicely.

00:17:14.201 --> 00:17:15.827
They are also surrounding the control room.

00:17:15.827 --> 00:17:18.205
Yes...

00:17:18.205 --> 00:17:19.206
Is something wrong?

00:17:19.206 --> 00:17:22.334
Don't you think this is going too smoothly?

00:17:24.211 --> 00:17:25.754
I do.

00:17:25.754 --> 00:17:27.881
However, that's not enough of a
reason for us to slacken our attack.

00:17:27.881 --> 00:17:30.342
You're right...

00:17:30.342 --> 00:17:32.177
Proceed as planned.

00:17:32.177 --> 00:17:32.886
Yes, ma'am.

00:17:42.771 --> 00:17:45.148
Kaboom! Another one gone.

00:17:45.148 --> 00:17:47.234
What a waste.

00:17:47.234 --> 00:17:49.778
Oh, here he comes.

00:17:49.778 --> 00:17:52.781
Quite a beauty, just like the rumors said.

00:17:52.781 --> 00:17:56.326
Well, if it wasn't, this wouldn't
be a profitable investment.

00:17:56.326 --> 00:17:57.244
Oops, almost forgot.

00:17:57.244 --> 00:17:59.663
Yu Fang, get ready!

00:17:59.663 --> 00:18:01.248
I already am.

00:18:01.248 --> 00:18:03.458
Yu Lan, how are you doing over there?

00:18:03.458 --> 00:18:04.668
You're not scared, are you?

00:18:04.668 --> 00:18:06.879
Oh! Sorry, sorry, you
can't talk right now, can you?

00:18:06.879 --> 00:18:09.173
I didn't do it on purpose, honest!

00:18:09.173 --> 00:18:12.885
My younger sister does not feel fear.

00:18:12.885 --> 00:18:14.052
I suppose not.

00:18:44.458 --> 00:18:45.876
This is Team Topaz.

00:18:45.876 --> 00:18:48.670
We're in front of the treasure chest.
Preparations complete.

00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:53.800
This is Team Ruby. We're in position as well.
Ready when you are.

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:56.720
This is strange.
It's too quiet.

00:18:56.720 --> 00:18:59.890
But there aren't any traps
or anything like that.

00:19:02.809 --> 00:19:05.729
Uruz 2 to Ruby and Topaz.

00:19:05.729 --> 00:19:08.440
Get ready to go in.
On the count of three...

00:19:08.440 --> 00:19:09.650
Two...

00:19:09.650 --> 00:19:10.442
One...

00:19:10.442 --> 00:19:11.276
Go!

00:19:28.961 --> 00:19:30.796
Clear.

00:19:30.796 --> 00:19:31.713
Clear.

00:19:31.713 --> 00:19:35.384
Or rather, there are only the hostages here.
No sign of the enemy.

00:19:35.384 --> 00:19:36.426
Any traps?

00:19:36.426 --> 00:19:37.427
No.

00:19:37.427 --> 00:19:40.556
It seems perfectly safe, but still...

00:19:40.556 --> 00:19:43.267
Wait there. I'm coming over.

00:19:43.267 --> 00:19:45.352
Are you sure you want to
get out of your machine?

00:19:45.352 --> 00:19:47.020
It should be fine now.

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:49.439
I've configured my AS to
automatically attack any AS units

00:19:49.439 --> 00:19:52.234
that do not respond to my IFF.

00:19:52.234 --> 00:19:54.862
Topaz, you patrol the perimeter.

00:19:54.862 --> 00:19:56.822
Topaz, understood.

00:19:58.365 --> 00:20:01.827
Well, it's about time.
Don't take it personally, okay?

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:11.336
Mike 2 destroyed.
Switching to search mode.

00:20:11.336 --> 00:20:13.046
This is weird, though...

00:20:13.046 --> 00:20:14.548
What is?

00:20:14.548 --> 00:20:16.216
They're not putting up enough of a fight.

00:20:16.216 --> 00:20:21.388
They're just old Savage models, so you
could say that's all there is to them, but...

00:20:21.388 --> 00:20:23.807
Agreed. Compared to the
complicated maneuvers

00:20:23.807 --> 00:20:25.475
those AS units pulled off
during the abduction,

00:20:25.475 --> 00:20:27.728
the techniques used by these Savages
we destroyed were way too simple.

00:20:27.728 --> 00:20:29.396
You thought so too, Sousuke?

00:20:29.396 --> 00:20:30.355
Yeah.

00:20:30.355 --> 00:20:32.482
You still haven't spotted
any enemy artillery?

00:20:32.482 --> 00:20:35.110
Yeah, that's right. Something stinks.

00:20:35.110 --> 00:20:37.821
Once we've seen what there is to see,
let's get out of here, fast.

00:20:37.821 --> 00:20:40.866
There you go. You'll be all right now, miss.

00:20:42.367 --> 00:20:45.537
It's not a chemical weapon
trap or anything like that...

00:20:45.537 --> 00:20:47.497
I mean, the air
conditioning is still working...

00:20:47.497 --> 00:20:50.167
Hey, this really is weird!

00:20:50.167 --> 00:20:52.002
What? What's wrong?

00:20:52.002 --> 00:20:54.505
There isn't anybody inside the
enemy AS unit I destroyed.

00:20:54.505 --> 00:20:56.089
It's empty!

00:20:56.089 --> 00:20:58.050
Was it controlled remotely or something?

00:20:58.050 --> 00:21:00.052
What in the hell is going on...

00:21:08.644 --> 00:21:09.978
What was that?

00:21:09.978 --> 00:21:11.605
Uruz 6, I don't copy...

00:21:11.605 --> 00:21:13.065
Repeat!

00:21:13.065 --> 00:21:14.650
What's going on with Kurz?

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:16.026
Uruz 6!

00:21:35.963 --> 00:21:37.756
What is happening?

00:21:37.756 --> 00:21:38.966
I do not know.

00:21:38.966 --> 00:21:42.511
The communication line is bad,
so I'm not getting any response...

00:21:42.511 --> 00:21:45.097
No, please wait. I might be able to...

00:21:45.097 --> 00:21:46.807
I've gotten through!

00:21:46.807 --> 00:21:48.600
Uruz 7 to HQ.

00:21:48.600 --> 00:21:50.978
Do you read me? Uruz 7 to HQ!

00:21:50.978 --> 00:21:53.605
This is HQ. What is your situation?

00:21:53.605 --> 00:21:56.400
The worst possible scenario has happened.

00:21:56.400 --> 00:21:59.069
It seems we've managed to walk into a trap.

00:22:04.491 --> 00:22:05.868
Venom.

00:22:09.496 --> 00:22:11.498
Hello there.

00:22:27.764 --> 00:22:29.516
<i>I'm sure you're still looking</i>

00:22:29.516 --> 00:22:33.312
<i>Straight ahead to tomorrow</i>

00:22:33.312 --> 00:22:39.193
<i>Just like you always have</i>

00:22:39.193 --> 00:22:44.907
<i>Just like the sunflowers</i>

00:22:44.907 --> 00:22:51.663
<i>That bloomed on that windy hill</i>

00:22:53.582 --> 00:22:59.505
<i>No matter how far apart we are</i>

00:22:59.505 --> 00:23:05.511
<i>I pray that my singing will reach you</i>

00:23:05.511 --> 00:23:11.558
<i>On nights when the tears never seem to stop</i>

00:23:11.558 --> 00:23:14.895
<i>I want to be the moon</i>

00:23:14.895 --> 00:23:17.898
<i>That shines through your window</i>

00:23:17.898 --> 00:23:25.948
<i>Because I believe we will meet again</i>

00:23:28.283 --> 00:23:31.870
<i>No matter what</i>

00:23:45.175 --> 00:23:46.134
"Next Episode"

00:23:46.134 --> 00:23:48.262
<i>A double, no, triple trap lying in wait.</i>

00:23:48.262 --> 00:23:52.975
<i>Venom. Shadow. Numerous venomous</i>
<i>fangs awaken from their slumber.</i>

00:23:52.975 --> 00:23:56.895
<i>We're cut off from escape, and the one</i>
<i>shooting at us is a ghost from the past.</i>

00:23:56.895 --> 00:23:59.022
<i>Next time: "Daylight."</i>

00:23:59.022 --> 00:24:00.649
<i>A dangerous ad-lib begins in the darkness,</i>

00:24:00.649 --> 00:24:04.672
<i>so that we can live</i>
<i>to see the daylight again.</i>
